      "id": "8lnpcq7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Force"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Force is a vector quantity defined as an push or pull that can alter an object's state of rest, motion, direction, or shape.",
        "Newton's Laws of Motion describe the relationship between a body and the forces acting upon it, establishing concepts of Inertia (1st Law), Momentum and F = ma (2nd Law), and Action-Reaction (3rd Law).",
        "Work is done when a force causes displacement in the direction of the force (W = F × s × cos θ), and it can be positive, negative, or zero.",
        "Power represents the rate at which work is done or energy is transferred (P = W / t)."
      ],
      "id": "a3p4u8l"
    },
